   "key": "federal-representatives-7372",
   "date": "2021-08-09",
   "house": "representatives",
   "question": "The majority voted in favour of *disagreeing* with an [amendment](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debates/?id=2021-08-09.102.2) introduced by Rankin MP [Jim Chalmers](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/rankin/jim_chalmers) (Labor), which means the amendment failed. ### Amendment text > *That all words after \"That\" be omitted with a view to substituting the following words:* > > *\"the [second reading](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/bills-and-laws/making-a-law-in-the-australian-parliament/) be considered immediately\".* To read a bill for a second time is to agree with the bill's main idea. ### Original motion text > *That the second reading be made an order of the day for the next sitting.*",
